      "title": "File handle leaked in sha helper",
      "message": "The file opened by p.open('rb') is never closed. It is called on many large archives, so file handles leak until GC. Also, hashlib.file_digest requires Python 3.11+, which the release notes (which only require Python 3) do not state.",
      "suggestion": "Use a with block to close the file, and document or check the Python 3.11+ requirement.",
      "confidence": 0.55,
